{"Race condition in counter increment - the read-modify-write operation on match_count is not atomic, causing lost increments under concurrent load leading to inaccurate statistics": 0.6298157572746277, "Security bypass in whitelist/blacklist check - regex without end-of-string anchor allows attacker to register with 'user@vaynermedia.com.evil.com' when whitelist is set to 'vaynermedia.com'": 0.8586797118186951, "State leak from mutable property on controller prototype - initializing a mutable array (Em.A([])) on a prototype means all instances share the same array, causing rejected emails from one attempt to affect all subsequent attempts since Ember controllers are singletons": 0.9127234220504761, "Case-sensitive email uniqueness validation allows duplicate accounts - uniqueness: true is case-sensitive by default, permitting registration of emails differing only by case which contradicts the case-insensitive email_hash method": 0.6981235146522522, "Inconsistent nullability for timestamp columns - t.timestamps creates nullable columns on Rails versions prior to 5.0, inconsistent with other columns explicitly defined with null: false": 0.13106687366962433, "Shared mutable array across all controller instances - Em.A([]) is evaluated once at class-definition time producing a single array object shared by every instance, causing previously-blocked emails to appear invalid immediately when modal is reopened": 0.9298086166381836, "Missing basic email format validation after refactor - EmailValidator only checks whitelist/blacklist domains and BlockedEmail.should_block but performs no RFC-format check, allowing malformed strings like 'notanemail' to be persisted": 0.7461872100830078}